# =========================================
# ACT II: The Five Lights of the Lantern Realm
# =========================================

label act_2_start:

    scene bg_act_2_start
    with fade
    play music "lantern_theme.ogg" fadein 2.0

    "The air shimmered like glass as the boys stood at the edge of a floating cliff."
    "Beneath them stretched a vast world of drifting islands and rivers of light winding through endless twilight."
    "Far away, a single tower rose from the horizon — its peak crowned with a faint, flickering glow."

    p "There it is, my brave young companions — the Great Beacon. Heart of the Lantern Realm."
    p "Once, its light filled every corner of this world. It kept the stars bright, the dreams alive, and the shadows asleep."

    "Pipwick adjusted his tiny waistcoat and polished the soot-stained lantern he carried. The flame inside guttered, fighting to stay alive."

    p "But now the Beacon weakens. Five guardian lanterns, each tied to a pillar of the realm’s harmony, have gone dark."
    p "Without them, the Beacon cannot hold against the dark that creeps from the edges of unlit space."

    t "So, what do we do?"
    p "You must find each lantern, mend what’s broken, and rekindle its flame."
    p "Only then will the Beacon’s heart burn bright enough to restore balance."

    h "Five lanterns...? That's a lot of walking."
    t "Better than staying here till the world breaks apart."
    h "If that's even really going to happen."

    "Pipwick gave a nervous chuckle and tugged at his collar, the metal buckles on his satchel clinking softly."

    p "Oh, thankfully the walking will be kept to a minimum."
    p "Each lantern possesses the ability to teleport you to the next region!"
    p "So you won’t have to trek across the entire realm."

    h "Okay, that's more like it."
    t "But... how will we know where to go?"

    p "You will not be alone! Each lantern is watched over by a guardian spirit — echoes of those you love most."
    p "Their light endures here because love endures everywhere. You’ll recognize them, though they may not remember you at first."

    "The brothers exchanged a glance — equal parts awe and uncertainty."

    t "So our family’s out there too?"
    p "In a manner of speaking. Fragments of them, shaped by the Lantern Realm’s memory of your hearts."
    h "That sounds… kinda creepy."
    p "Touching and ethereal, my boy, not creepy! Language matters!"

    "Pipwick straightened his vest and tapped the lantern’s frame twice. It flared faintly, casting a narrow path of gold across the clouds."

    p "Follow its glow — it will guide you to the first lantern’s resting place."
    p "The path resolves at the Luminous Library."

    t "I think we should do it, Henry."
    h "Together, right?"
    t "Together."

    "The boys nodded, determination gleaming in their eyes."
    "They stepped forward together, the lantern’s light stretching ahead like a thread through the clouds."

    p "Onward, Twin Sparks! The fate of the Lantern Realm rests in your hands."

    jump region_1_library



